CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12 --unwind 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ lock while alive: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ lock after expiry: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ unordered_map: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ what: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
no body for callee
dropped the body
--
The models follow libc++ 18's src/memory.cpp, src/hash.cpp, src/new.cpp and
the exception fallback; what() strings are implementation-defined.
